Two parts of the operations request are not included. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich` would need `http-client`, which is also not granted. The world therefore has no import that could do either, and adding one would widen the node's authority beyond its declared contract. If operations wants those behaviours, the graph's `with` clause needs to grant the capabilities, for example through a separate logging node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        let knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
